			<div class="content" id="post-content-2394225">
									

<p>This is all sorts of excellent - Jessica is a lesson in how to provide some character without backstory, and the anomaly opens up lots of questions and further thought, which is great.</p>
<p>I would suggest changing the designations of the addenda / interviews, as I find it mildly distracting that they are -1 / -2 in the same way as parts of the anomaly.</p>
<p>My one tiny issue is that I struggle to believe that the second interview was written by -2. Those turns of phrase sound much more like speech than writing, and it's a lot of writing to do at once, without being interrupted by more questions from the interviewer. And it makes more sense for the cawing to prevent further speech than further writing. Is there a reason that interview couldn't be spoken?</p>

