<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><br />
Maybe. Deckard owns a synthetic sheep and dreams about it, but it isn't really ever clear if Deckard is an android. The V.K. test he failed was administered by androids masquerading as police officers, and may have been fraudulent. Or not. That's kind of the point.</p>
<p>There's a reasonable interpretation of the book that humanity is nearly extinct and <em>everyone</em> in the novel is synthetic, except for Isidore. This is symbolized by the toad Deckard finds at the end of the book and thinks is a real animal, thought to be extinct, but is discovered to be synthetic.</p>
</div>
